---
import CallToBook from "../components/CallToBook.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Policies | Team Battle Ready Gaming Trailer"
  description="Draft deposit, cancellation, weather, food, and damage rules for Team Battle Ready gaming trailer bookings in Central Texas."
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Draft policy" title="The rules, in plain English." crumb="Policies">
    <p>
      This is the launch draft, dated October 6, 2026. It is not legal advice. Soft launch holds the date by phone.
    </p>
  </PageHero>

  <article class="section prose" style="padding-top: 0.5rem">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Deposit</h2>
      <p>
        The deposit is a flat $100 on every booking: Skirmish, Mission, Campaign, a 6- or 8-hour full day, and the Monday–Thursday rate for verified organizations. That hourly rate is for schools, churches, units, and nonprofits with a tax-exempt certificate or a purchase order. It is not a home-party price. Add-ons, travel, tax, and the $25 discount do not change the deposit.
      </p>
      <p>
        Prices on the card exclude tax. Quotes and booking totals add 8.25% to the subtotal. The $100 deposit comes off that tax-included total.
      </p>
      <p>
        Call or text (254) 251-5219 to arrange the $100 deposit. The balance is due before the event. Cash or Zelle on arrival is fine when you agree to it on the call.
      </p>
      <h2>Cancellation</h2>
      <p>Cancel 14 or more days before the event and the deposit is refunded in full.</p>
      <p>Cancel 3 to 13 days out and the deposit becomes a credit good for 12 months. It is not returned as cash.</p>
      <p>Cancel inside 72 hours and the deposit is forfeited.</p>
      <h2>Weather</h2>
      <p>
        Rain alone does not cancel. The cabin is climate-controlled on purpose. Lightning, ice, winds above 35 mph, or a National Weather Service warning: you get a free reschedule or a full credit. You choose.
      </p>
      <h2>Late start</h2>
      <p>
        The clock starts at the scheduled time. If parking or access is not ready, the coach waits up to 30 minutes. Time lost after that is not added to the back of the event, because the next slot may belong to someone else.
      </p>
      <h2>Travel</h2>
      <p>
        Travel is free within 30 miles, $50 for 31–45 miles, and $90 for 46–60 miles. Past 60 miles is a quote, with no published fee. The town list is on the <a href="/areas">areas page</a>. A fee that was wrong because we mis-measured the address gets fixed. A fee that changes because the storage lot moves gets fixed on the site before new bookings, not after.
      </p>
      <h2>Food, drink, and gum</h2>
      <p>They stay outside the trailer. A violation is a $75 cleaning fee on this draft.</p>
      <h2>Damage</h2>
      <p>Damage is billed at replacement cost to the card on file. Normal wear on a controller is not damage. A broken screen is.</p>
      <h2>Ratings and supervision</h2>
      <p>
        The host sets the game-rating limit and is responsible for telling us. The coach enforces the limit you set. The host also supplies any adult supervision the venue requires beyond the coach.
      </p>
      <h2>Photos</h2>
      <p>
        Photos of an event go on a social feed only with the booking host’s consent. Say so on the booking if faces should stay off.
      </p>
      <h2>Discounts</h2>
      <p>
        Military, first responders, and teachers: $25 off the package price, or off the Monday–Thursday hourly total. Bring an ID. The $25 does not come off travel, add-ons, or extra time.
      </p>
      <h2>On post</h2>
      <p>
        Fort Cavazos bookings still depend on installation access. We do not guarantee a gate we do not control. We do not use official seals, and we do not speak for the installation.
      </p>
      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        The version that applies is the one you accept at booking. If this page changes later, existing deposits keep the rules from the day they were paid.
      </p>
      <p><CallToBook /></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
